"""Deli Counter 0.247.0 (the factory's roadmap 148): a corner store's selling floor stands its aisle gondolas in rows.

The look review of 2026-10-19 found the rooms "Too sparse"; deli_a03's market aisles were 300 m2 with 5.7 % of the
floor under anything standing. A corner store's selling floor (`level_design.is_corner_store_floor`: a deli, a
convenience store or a gas station, its `market`, `aisles` or `sales` room) now lays rows of Zoo's `snack_gondola`
down its long axis -- or along its own aisles, at their depth and on their line -- with the contract's 1.25 m aisle
round every gondola, until a quarter of the floor stands under furniture or nothing more clears. A deli is a store to
`migrate_store_gondolas.py`, so its two authored aisle shelves are snack gondolas too.

What this writes, every target pinned by its hash and refused on a mismatch, nothing written until every file has
been worked out: `level_design.py`, `presets.py`, `migrate_store_gondolas.py`, `test_furnish.py` and
`test_store_gondolas.py` (anchored hunks); the 14 specs the rows refurnish, carried whole; the new
`test_corner_store_rows.py`; VERSION; the CHANGELOG entry, prepended. Generated from a proven clone
(`patches/dc_corner_store_rows/gen_dc_corner_store_rows.py`), dry-run on a fresh clone to the clone's every byte, a
second run refused (`patches/dc_corner_store_rows/dry_run_*.out.txt`).

    python patches/patch_dc_corner_store_rows.py
    cd deli_counter && python build.py --all && python -m pytest -q && python check.py
"""
